<title>UK: Sterling Publishing up after newspaper tip.</title>
<headline>Sterling Publishing up after newspaper tip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's Sterling Publishing Group Plc climbed on Wednesday after the Daily Mail newspaper said the company was set to return to profit.</p>
<p>The newspaper said Sterling would announce annual profits of 2.5 million stg for the year to March 31. It made a pre-tax loss of 3.48 million the previous year.</p>
<p>The shares were 2-1/2p higher at 22p by 1338 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
